# Terraform
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/terraform.tfvars
**/tfplan
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup

# Week subdirectory .github folders (workflows live at repo root)
week-*/.github/

# Blog HTML files (kept locally only)
**/docs/blog/*.html
**/docs/blog/BLOG_BLOGGER.html
# Legacy paths (pre-restructure)
week-*/blog/*.html
week-*/blog/BLOG_BLOGGER.html

# LinkedIn post drafts (personal working files — screenshots need to be
# public for the blog's raw.githubusercontent.com embeds, these don't)
**/docs/linkedin/

# Lambda build artifacts (generated by Terraform archive_file — never commit zips)
**/lambda/builds/
**/lambda_layer/
**/*.zip

# Exception: Week 6 is HCP/VCS-driven (not local CLI apply), so its Lambda
# zips must be committed for the remote run to find them — see
# week-06-account-vending-machine/.gitignore for the rationale.
!week-06-account-vending-machine/lambda/*/*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Local study and prep docs (not for GitHub)
**/docs/explainer.md
**/docs/blog-prep.md
**/docs/commands.md
**/docs/screenshots.md
**/docs/screenshots-guide.md
**/docs/readme-with-screenshots.md
**/docs/execution-guide.md
# Legacy paths (pre-restructure)
**/EXPLAINER.md
**/BLOG_PREP.md
**/README-with-screenshots.md
**/COMMANDS.md
**/SCREENSHOTS.md

# Blog screenshots are committed to GitHub — needed for raw.githubusercontent.com CDN in blog posts

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
SESSION_CONTEXT.md
SESSION_ARCHIVE.md
WEEK_TEMPLATE.md
BRIEFINGS.md

# ServiceNow credentials — local only, read by scripts/servicenow/*.py, never committed
.servicenow.env

# Playwright persistent browser profile — contains AWS Console/HCP/ServiceNow
# login session cookies, local only, read by scripts/screenshots/capture.py
playwright_profile/

# Exported browser cookies (Cookie-Editor JSON, etc.) — local only, read once
# by scripts/screenshots/import_cookies.py, delete after import if desired
*cookies*.json

# Local MCP client config - points at an ephemeral Function URL that changes
# on every apply, so it is machine-specific rather than shared.
.mcp.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Untracked-but-present paths, ignored explicitly after 2026-09-05.
#
# A `git add -A` from the repo root staged all of these and pushed them to a
# PUBLIC repo: 20,000 node_modules files, local scratch projects, working
# notes and two .env files. They were never secret -- the .env files hold a
# Vite feature flag and an API URL, both of which ship in a browser bundle
# anyway -- but none of it belongs in this repository.
#
# Being untracked was not protection. `git add -A` stages untracked files by
# design. Being ignored is protection.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local assistant config and notes
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Separate projects that happen to live under this root
bedrock-secure-model-invocation-api/
finops-ebs-savings-tracker/
ebs-savings-dashboard/

# Browser automation profiles used for screenshots
playwright_profile_batch/

# Build and run detritus
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
throwaway.png
**/out.json
**/docs/repost-draft.md

# Environment files, everywhere, always
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
